---
import FlowShot from '../FlowShot.astro';
import FlowDetail from '../FlowDetail.astro';
import shotBanner from '../../../assets/flow/shots/flow-expand-run-banner-shot.webp';
import detailConsent from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-expand-consent.webp';
import detailSaved from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-expand-saved.webp';
---
<section class="border-t border-border/60 px-6 py-14 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="tour-expand">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="of-eyebrow" data-animate="rise">Expand with Sources</p>
      <h3 id="tour-expand" class="of-display scroll-mt-28 mt-4 text-[clamp(1.85rem,3.4vw,2.75rem)]" data-animate="lead">See the agent work. Stop it when you want.</h3>
      <p class="of-lede mt-5" data-animate="rise">
        Expand can read the document and search folders you opened. Flow names each lookup as
        it happens, counts real tokens and cost, and keeps pause and stop in reach. The final
        writing still returns through the same review and approval path.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted" data-animate="rise">
        Today, lookups use hosted Anthropic models only. The text leaves your Mac, fetching public
        pages stays switched off, and every run stops at its limit of 12 lookups or 180 seconds.
        If it reaches that bound, nothing in the document was changed.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-12" data-animate="plate">
      <FlowShot src={shotBanner} alt="Orionfold Flow during Expand with Sources: a banner lists folder searches as they happen, tokens and dollars accrue in the title bar, and pause and stop remain available." caption="Every lookup narrated live · Pause or stop in one click" natural sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 78rem, (min-width: 1024px) 64rem, 100vw" />
    </div>
    <div class="mx-auto mt-12 grid max-w-5xl gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <p class="flow-path__num">Consent</p>
        <h4 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">Destination, sources, estimate, authority.</h4>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">The sheet names what will leave, where it will go, and the estimated cost to the digit. Permission is read-only and granted once.</p>
        <FlowDetail class="mt-6" src={detailConsent} alt="Flow's Leaves this Mac sheet naming Anthropic, the included sources, an exact estimate, read-only authority, and Allow Once." caption="The complete bargain · Before the run" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 30rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="flow-path__num">Receipt</p>
        <h4 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">Estimate before. Recorded cost after.</h4>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">One measured run estimated 0.000924 USD and later recorded 0.026684 USD. Those are two facts, kept separate. The saved change is bound to its before-and-after fingerprints.</p>
        <FlowDetail class="mt-6" src={detailSaved} alt="A Flow receipt showing recorded cost, model, provider, cloud route, before and after digests, and Receipt valid." caption="Recorded cost · Exact saved change · Receipt valid" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 30rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)" glow />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
